      "math_academy_id": "e-121",
      "problem": "Find the average rate of change of the function $f(x)$ on the interval $[-1,2]$ given the following table of values for $f(x)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n| $x$ | $\\,-1\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,2\\,$ | $\\,3\\,$ | $\\,4\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\,-3\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,1\\,$ | $\\,6\\,$ | $\\,0\\,$ | $\\,4\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the average rate of change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(2)-f(-1)}{2-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-(-3)}{2-(-1)} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
